{
  "metadata": {
    "protocol": "Day 1 training only. Evaluated using exact frozen model hyperparameters: KNeighborsClassifier(n_neighbors=5, weights='distance'), subsampled to 25,000 Day 1 train flows (seed 42). Signed log1p: sign(x) * log1p(|x|) on continuous heavy-tailed features, StandardScaler on train only, z-scores clipped to [-5.0, +5.0].",
    "explanation_baseline_difference": "The earlier KNN preprocessing table reported AUC 0.9893 and calibrated FPR 1.60% because it instantiated KNeighborsClassifier with default uniform weights (weights='uniform') on the full 170,884 un-subsampled train set. The frozen model (models/knn.joblib, checksum 3046dcae...) uses distance weighting (weights='distance') fitted on a 25,000-flow Day 1 subsample, which outputs continuous distance-weighted posteriors rather than 6 discrete probabilities, yielding AUC 0.9954 and calibrated FPR 0.36% (at threshold 0.8200) on Cross-Day test.",
    "negative_values_handling_log1p": "log1p(x) is mathematically undefined for x <= -1. To robustly handle negative values (such as -1 in Init_Win_bytes and negative timing/header artifacts like -2.12e9 in Bwd Header Length), we apply the continuous, odd signed log1p: signed_log1p(x) = sign(x) * log(1 + |x|). This maps 0 to 0, x > 0 to log(1 + x), and negative values to -log(1 + |x|) without producing NaNs, dampening extreme negative outliers while preserving polarity.",
    "heavy_tailed_features_full_25": [
      "Bwd Packets/s",
      "Down/Up Ratio",
      "Bwd Packet Length Mean",
      "Bwd Packet Length Max",
      "Init_Win_bytes_forward",
